course: dictionary
lesson: 8702
title: The semicolon
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A semicolon ; is a punctuation mark. It joins two full sentences that are closely linked, so it sits between two ideas that belong together. «It was raining; we stayed in.» Each side could stand alone as a sentence, and the semicolon shows that the two ideas are connected.
explain: A semicolon is stronger than a comma but weaker than a full stop. Use it when a full stop would cut the link too sharply. If one side could not stand alone as a sentence, the semicolon is wrong there.
explain: A semicolon can also sort a long list when the items already have commas inside them. «We visited Paris, France; Rome, Italy; and Madrid, Spain.» Without semicolons, the commas inside each place would be confusing.
fact: A semicolon is the punctuation mark ;.
fact: A semicolon joins two full sentences that are closely linked, such as «It was raining; we stayed in.»
fact: Joining two full sentences with only a comma is a comma splice, and it is wrong.
fact: A semicolon can separate items in a long list when the items already contain commas.
fact: Many computer programming languages end each line of code with a semicolon.
exercise: «It was raining; we stayed in.» What is the semicolon doing? | It starts a list of names | It asks a question | It ends the whole story | *It joins two full sentences that belong together
exercise: Which sentence uses a semicolon correctly? | It was late; because. | It was; late I went home. | It was late; went home. | *It was late; I went home.
exercise: Which sentence uses a semicolon to sort a list whose items already contain commas? | We visited Paris, France, Rome, Italy; and Madrid, Spain; yes. | *We visited Paris, France; Rome, Italy; and Madrid, Spain. | We visited; Paris, France, Rome, Italy. | We visited Paris; France, Rome; Italy, Madrid; Spain.
test: What is wrong with «It was raining, we stayed in.»? | *It joins two full sentences with only a comma, which is a comma splice | It is a question with no question mark | It has a semicolon in the wrong place | It has too many words
test: Which mark could replace the comma in «It was raining, we stayed in.»? | a hyphen | an apostrophe | a question mark | *a semicolon
exam: Which sentence uses a semicolon correctly? | The shop was closed; walked home instead. | The shop was closed; because. | The shop was; closed we walked home. | *The shop was closed; we walked home instead.
